  "title": "The (k−1)-Tournament Schütte Boundary: f(k−1,k) = k+3",
  "batch_label": "87",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer k >= 3, f(k-1,k) = k+3 under the common-outside-vertex and common-tournament quantifiers frozen in source.md. The proof also establishes the required structural lemma: for every tournament T on V with |V| = n >= 3, define ab to be an edge of H_T exactly when a beats every vertex of V other than a,b or b beats every vertex of V other than a,b; then H_T is contained in a star or is exactly a triangle.",
